      "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "(1 in a multiple picture album)<br>\nThis is the first view of Randsburg which is about 2 miles off of CA Hwy 395.  Up in the right are the tailings of the Yellow Aster Mine. The first placer gold was found in 1893 and then the Astor mine began operating in 1895. The gold began running out in the 1930s.  Silver was also found and the Kelly Mine operated until the 40s. $20 million in gold was taken out of this area.",
